From 47eccb8b3fc63a74347ea898f5f7fc22d711e9c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lauri Ojansivu <x@xet7.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:09:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Release files of any size by default.

[repository.release] FILE_MAX_SIZE is -1, no limit, by default (it was
2048 MB): a release is as large as what it releases, and a mirror of
another forge's releases has no say in their sizes. A configured limit is
kept.

A negative limit was not usable before, so two places are fixed with it:

- an API upload streamed as application/octet-stream wrapped the body in
  http.MaxBytesReader with the negative limit, which Go takes as 0, so
  every byte was refused; the reader is used only for a limit of 0 or more.
- the upload form passed the limit to Dropzone as maxFilesize, and a
  negative maxFilesize refuses every file, while without one Dropzone
  applies its own 256 MiB; dropzoneMaxFilesize gives Dropzone 0, which it
  takes as no limit, for a limit of 0 or less.

Tests: TestLoadRepositoryReleaseFileMaxSize, TestUploadAttachmentSizeLimit
(known size and streamed, with and without a limit) and dropzone.test.ts.
---
